@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# ZERONYTH / Besu 26.9.0 — Falcon-1024 QBFT work-in-progress
+
+This is a **research fork patch**, not a completed Falcon-only QBFT client.
+
+## Verified in an isolated build
+
+- Temurin JDK 25.0.5+8; `bcprov-jdk18on` 1.84.
+- Bouncy Castle Falcon-1024 generation, signing and verification are real, not mocks.
+- Five separate domain-separated signature purposes: PROPOSAL, PREPARE, COMMIT,
+  ROUND_CHANGE and BLOCK COMMIT SEAL.
+- Signature context includes chain ID, height, round and 32-byte canonical payload digest.
+- A strict experimental wire envelope authenticates a recomputed payload hash using a
+  genesis/active-set allowlist of exact Falcon-1024 public keys; an arbitrary sender-supplied
+  key is insufficient.
+- Tests reject signature modification, unknown signer, wrong chain, wrong round,
+  wrong height, wrong message type, truncation and appended data.
+- `Falcon1024CommitQuorum` provides a reusable strict, fail-closed validator commit-seal
+  threshold check (`floor(2N/3)+1`) with exact chain, block, round and signer binding.
+- A **simulated** 4-key quorum test accepts 3/4 signatures, rejects 2/4,
+  rejects duplicates, unknown keys, cross-chain/block/round replay, and duplicate
+  public keys in the active validator registry. **These are not four Besu processes.**
+- `FalconQbftPayloadAuthenticator` converts **real native QBFT Payload** hashes
+  to/from the experimental Falcon envelope; it is not yet invoked in message networking.
+
+## Not implemented or verified yet
+
+1. `MessageFactory`/`QbftMessageDecoder` dispatch to Falcon-only v2 messages.
+2. `SignedData` and `BftMessage` native signed-message data flow using Falcon instead of
+   `SECPSignature` and secp256k1 sender recovery.
+3. Validator-set identity binding throughout proposer selection, address lookup and
+   dynamic validator membership. New experimental genesis keys are required; existing
+   ECDSA validator addresses are **not** interchangeable with Falcon-derived identities.
+4. `CommitPayload`, `QbftRound`, `RoundState`, `BftExtraData`, `QbftExtraDataCodec`,
+   `BftBlockHashing`, `CommitValidator` and header seal verification must carry and
+   validate Falcon commit seals, not `SECPSignature` objects.
+5. Fully rebuilding Besu 26.9.0, integration tests and four real Besu processes.
+6. Chaos tests, throughput, sync/restart and production VPS staging/deployment.
+
+**The live Chain ID 9127 network remains ECDSA-based QBFT with its independent ML-DSA-65
+proof layer. None of this work has been deployed to that chain.**
+
+Retain the separate ML-DSA-65 proof layer. EVM-wallet secp256k1 transaction signatures
+are a different trust boundary and should not be removed as part of QBFT authentication.
+
+## Changed/added files (relative to Besu 26.9.0)
+
+- `crypto/algorithms/src/main/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024ConsensusCrypto.java`
+- `crypto/algorithms/src/main/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024ConsensusEnvelope.java`
+- `crypto/algorithms/src/main/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024CommitQuorum.java`
+- `crypto/algorithms/src/test/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024ConsensusCryptoTest.java`
+- `crypto/algorithms/src/test/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024ConsensusCryptoSelfTest.java`
+- `crypto/algorithms/src/test/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024QuorumSelfTest.java`
+- `consensus/qbft-core/src/main/java/org/hyperledger/besu/consensus/qbft/core/payload/FalconQbftPayloadAuthenticator.java`
+- `consensus/qbft-core/build.gradle` (adds crypto:algorithms dependency)
+
+## Repeatable standalone cryptographic smoke tests
+
+With JDK 25 and an authorized `bcprov-jdk18on-1.84.jar` available locally:
+
+```bash
+BC_JAR=/path/to/bcprov-jdk18on-1.84.jar
+TEST_OUT=/path/to/build-output
+mkdir -p "$TEST_OUT"
+javac -cp "$BC_JAR" -d "$TEST_OUT" \
+  crypto/algorithms/src/main/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024ConsensusCrypto.java \
+  crypto/algorithms/src/main/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024ConsensusEnvelope.java \
+  crypto/algorithms/src/main/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024CommitQuorum.java \
+  crypto/algorithms/src/test/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024ConsensusCryptoSelfTest.java \
+  crypto/algorithms/src/test/java/org/hyperledger/besu/crypto/Falcon1024QuorumSelfTest.java
+java -cp "$TEST_OUT:$BC_JAR" org.hyperledger.besu.crypto.Falcon1024ConsensusCryptoSelfTest
+java -cp "$TEST_OUT:$BC_JAR" org.hyperledger.besu.crypto.Falcon1024QuorumSelfTest
+```
+
+Besu's full Gradle build was attempted, but blocked by Gradle distribution DNS resolution;
+this patch has **not** passed a complete Besu build. The native QBFT adapter currently
+needs compile-time integration verification as well.
+
+Before deploying a Falcon-only experiment, allocate a **new genesis and network/protocol
+version**. Do not allow old ECDSA-based nodes to accept Falcon envelopes via implicit
+fallback or replace a live validator's key in place. Persist validator secret keys with
+encryption and restricted filesystem permissions. Audit cryptographic implementation and
+wire validation before use with anything of value.
-- 
